## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross‑protocol token exchanges, tenant isolation, and secure internal token issuance with revocation capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- RFC 8693 token exchange semantics
- Per‑tenant validation (issuer, audience, grant_type)
- Mutual TLS authentication for service clients
- PKCE/ROT flow enforcement where applicable
- Internal JWT issuance with per‑tenant signing keys
- Act claim for original token reference
- Tenant‑scoped revocation and audit stores

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal exchange flow (Express pseudo-code)
app.post('/token-exchange', async (req, res) => {
  const tenant = await getTenant(req.headers['x-tenant-id']);
  const incomingToken = await validateToken(req.body.token, tenant);
  const clientCert = req.socket.getPeerCertificate();

  if (!await validateClientCert(clientCert, tenant)) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'invalid_client' });
  }

  const internalJWT = await issueInternalJWT(incomingToken, tenant);
  await logExchange(tenant.id, incomingToken.jti, internalJWT.jti);

  res.json({ access_token: internalJWT, token_type: 'Bearer' });
});
```
